minion Bank is one of Canada's largest banks, with retail banking in Canada and the eastern United States, wealth management and capital markets. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 17.9% to C$67.8B in fiscal 2025 (ended Oct 31, 2025). Net interest income rose 8.5% to C$33.1B and noninterest income rose 28.5% to C$34.7B; noninterest expense fell 5.5%, and the provision for credit losses was C$4.5B, versus C$4.3B.","Net income to common rose 2.4× to C$20.0B, or C$11.56 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 57.0% versus 71.1%. TD Bank returned C$27.0B through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 17.9% to C$67.8B.","Net interest income rose 8.5%.","Noninterest income rose 28.5% to C$34.7B.","Net income to common rose 2.4× to C$20.0B."],"watch":["Credit-loss provision rose 5.9% to C$4.5B.","Deposits fell 0.5% to C$1.3T.","Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was C$38.6B, down 5.5%."],"table":[["Total revenue",67.777,57.497,1],["Net interest income",33.062,30.472],["Noninterest income",34.715,27.025],["Noninterest expense",38.637,40.871],["Provision for credit losses",4.506,4.253],["Other items, net",-0.686,-0.84],["Pre-tax income",23.948,11.533,1],["Income tax",3.41,2.691],["Preferred dividends & other",-0.565,0.526],["Net income to common",19.973,8.316,1],["Diluted EPS (C$)",11.56,4.72,0,"eps"],["Book value per share (C$)",73.790645,63.405519,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["The Toronto-Dominion Bank Form 40-F filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0000947263&type=40-F"],["TD Bank financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/td/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 49% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 49 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"C$67.8B","sub":"revenue · +17.9%","lines":["Net interest income C$33.1B","Noninterest income C$34.7B"],"cap":"Reven